I carry on telling Timo and Lena my story.
"At the airport I found a taxi," I say.
"I gave the driver my new address and paid for the journey."
"At the building I then saw the stairs."
"Unfortunately the flat does not have a lift."
Timo asks: "What did you do then?"
"I dragged my heavy suitcase up the stairs," I answer.
"I really carried it step by step."
"On the stairs I then suddenly heard a woman."
"She greeted me in a friendly way."
"So I met my neighbour Sabine right on the first day."
"Her little dog Bruno looked at me curiously."
"He immediately sniffed at my suitcase."
Timo and Lena laugh at this picture.
"You made friends right on the very first day!" Lena says.
I smile and nod.
I have really had luck in Berlin.
